    "contentUrl": "https://content.jwplatform.com/videos/uxVbJslB-K3AjnAEN.mp4",
    "description": "In this video, Chef John teaches you how to make an Easy Sweet and Sour Pork Belly using a simple method. He starts by scoring the pork belly and seasoning it with a mix of kosher salt, brown sugar, cayenne, and black pepper. Then, he roasts it in the oven covered with foil for 3 and a half hours at 250°F. After cooling and chilling it overnight, he slices it up and separates the fat and jelly left in the pan to use for the sweet and sour sauce. The result is a deliciously tender and flavorful pork belly that can be enjoyed as is or with a sauce.",
